+# PHASE A.5 — CI CONFIGURATION FIX REPORT
+
+**Repository:** `/workspace`  
+**Branch:** `feature/phase-a5-security-foundation`  
+**File modified:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml`  
+**Verification type:** Read-only audit + configuration fix (no application code changes)  
+**Status:** COMPLETE
+
+---
+
+## 1. Changes Made
+
+### Change 1: Fix PostgreSQL database name mismatch
+
+**Before:**
+```yaml
+services:
+  postgres:
+    env:
+      POSTGRES_DB: lead_pipeline
+env:
+  DATABASE_URL: postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/lead_pipeline_test
+```
+
+**After:**
+```yaml
+services:
+  postgres:
+    env:
+      POSTGRES_DB: lead_pipeline_test
+env:
+  DATABASE_URL: postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/lead_pipeline_test
+```
+
+**Reason:** The PostgreSQL service container was creating a database named `lead_pipeline`, but the application connects to `lead_pipeline_test`. This would cause `initDb()` to fail because the target database doesn't exist. Both now reference `lead_pipeline_test`.
+
+### Change 2: Remove hardcoded CI secrets and generate ephemeral values
+
+**Before:**
+```yaml
+env:
+  JWT_SECRET: lp-ci-test-secret-weak-but-test-only-32chars
+  ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY: aGVsbG8gd29ybGQgaGVsbG8gd29ybGQgaGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=
+```
+
+**After:** Removed from `env` block. Added a step that generates cryptographically random values at runtime:
+
+```yaml
+- name: Generate ephemeral test secrets
+  run: |
+    JWT_SECRET=$(node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))")
+    ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY=$(node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))")
+    echo "JWT_SECRET=$JWT_SECRET" >> $GITHUB_ENV
+    echo "ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY=$ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY" >> $GITHUB_ENV
+```
+
+**Reason:** Hardcoded secrets in version control are a security anti-pattern. The new approach:
+- Uses Node.js `crypto.randomBytes()` (cryptographically secure)
+- JWT secret: 48 bytes = 96 hex characters (well above the 32-character minimum required by the application's production validation)
+- Encryption master key: 32 bytes base64-encoded (exactly the 32-byte length required by `ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY` validation)
+- Values exported via `$GITHUB_ENV` so they're available to all subsequent steps (lint, build, server start, tests)
+- Values are NOT printed to stdout, so they don't appear in workflow logs
+
+### Change 3: Preserved safeguards (unchanged)
+
+| Safeguard | Status |
+|---|---|
+| PostgreSQL/Redis health checks | ✅ Unchanged |
+| `ALLOW_NETWORK: "false"` | ✅ Unchanged |
+| Test database name isolation (`lead_pipeline_test`) | ✅ Now consistent |
+| Fail-closed test DB guard in `server.js` | ✅ Unchanged |
+| Existing lint/build/test steps | ✅ Unchanged |
+
+---
+
+## 2. Verification Checks Executed
+
+| Check | Method | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| YAML syntax validation | Node.js structural parse | ✅ Valid |
+| POSTGRES_DB matches DATABASE_URL db name | `lead_pipeline_test` == `lead_pipeline_test` | ✅ Match |
+| Hardcoded secrets removed from env | No `JWT_SECRET` or `ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY` in `env` block | ✅ Removed |
+| Secrets generation step present | `Generate ephemeral test secrets` step found | ✅ Present |
+| `randomBytes` used for secret generation | Node.js `crypto.randomBytes()` | ✅ Used |
+| `$GITHUB_ENV` export mechanism | `echo "VAR=$VAL" >> $GITHUB_ENV` | ✅ Used |
+| `npm run lint` | `node --check server.js swagger.js vite.config.js` | ✅ Pass |
+| `npm run build` | `vite build` | ✅ Pass |
+| Unit tests (45 tests, 7 suites) | `node --test` with `DEMO_MODE=true NODE_ENV=test` | ✅ 45/45 pass |
+| `git diff --stat` | Only `ci.yml` modified | ✅ 9 insertions, 3 deletions |
+
