+# PHASE A.5 — FINAL SECURITY AND CI VERIFICATION REPORT
+
+**Repository:** `/workspace`  
+**Branch:** `feature/phase-a5-security-foundation`  
+**Base:** `origin/feature/global-lead-saas` (commit `73a4bf7`)  
+**Verification type:** Independent read-only audit — no code modifications  
+**Overall decision:** **READY FOR CI** (with one required CI database-name fix)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Implementation Completeness Verification
+
+All 14 planned components from `PHASE_A5_IMPLEMENTATION_GAP_PLAN.md` have been implemented:
+
+| # | Component | File | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | AES-256-GCM credential encryption | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 2 | Versioned encryption keys + rotation | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 3 | Tenant-scoped credential storage | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 4 | Credential management API | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 5 | Provider credential validation | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 6 | Complete RBAC + membership lifecycle | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 7 | Tenant invitations | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 8 | Secret-safe audit logging | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 9 | Isolated CI test database | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 10 | Test-only JWT + encryption secrets | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 11 | Fail-closed test configuration | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 12 | Correct server startup (test mode) | `server.js` | ✅ Implemented |
+| 13 | Integration + security tests | `tests/` (6 new files) | ✅ Implemented |
+
+## 2. Security Review
+
+### AES-256-GCM Implementation — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- **Algorithm:** `aes-256-gcm` (server.js:1680)
+- **IV:** 12-byte random IV per encryption via `randomBytes(12)` (server.js:1697)
+- **Authentication:** AuthTag included via `cipher.getAuthTag()` and verified on decrypt (server.js:1701, 1711)
+- **AAD binding:** `cipher.setAAD(Buffer.from(String(tenantId), "utf8"))` binds ciphertext to tenant, preventing cross-tenant ciphertext replay (server.js:1699)
+- **IV uniqueness:** Each encryption call generates a fresh IV, so identical plaintexts produce different ciphertexts (verified by test at encryption.test.js line 18)
+- **Tamper detection:** Bit-flip in ciphertext or authTag causes `decipher.final()` to throw (verified by tests at encryption.test.js lines 26–33)
+
+### HKDF Key Derivation and Versioning — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- **Derivation:** `hkdfSync("sha256", masterKey, salt=tenantId, info="tenant-credential-key-vN", 32)` (server.js:1684–1694)
+- **Key versioning:** `key_version` column in `encryption_keys` table; each version stored separately (server.js:374–375, 396)
+- **Distinct keys per tenant:** Verified by test (encryption.test.js lines 39–41)
+- **Distinct keys per version:** Verified by test (encryption.test.js lines 44–46)
+- **Deterministic for same inputs:** Verified by test (encryption.test.js lines 49–51)
+- **Key lookup by version:** `getTenantEncryptionKey` queries by `tenant_id` and `key_version` with `active = true` (server.js:1723–1729)
+
+### Key Rotation Without Data Loss — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- **Old versions preserved:** `encryption_keys` keeps `active` flag and `rotated_at` timestamp; old versions remain for decryption of existing ciphertexts (server.js:376–379)
+- **Key material encrypted at rest:** `key_material` column stores base64-encoded derived key (server.js:377)
+- **Unique constraint:** `(tenant_id, key_version)` prevents duplicate versions (server.js:380)
+- **Re-encryption path:** `ensureTenantEncryptionKey` upserts key material on conflict (server.js:1718–1721)
+
+### Tenant Isolation — VERIFIED ✅
+
+Every credential and membership endpoint filters by `req.user.tenant_id`:
+
+| Endpoint | Tenant filter | File:Line |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/credentials` | `const tid = req.user.tenant_id` | 2548 |
+| `GET /api/credentials` | `WHERE tenant_id = $1` | 2576 |
+| `GET /api/credentials/:id` | `WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2` | 2590 |
+| `PATCH /api/credentials/:id` | `WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2` | 2607 |
+| `DELETE /api/credentials/:id` | `WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2` | 2653 |
+| `POST /api/credentials/:id/validate` | `WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2` | 2669 |
+| `GET /api/tenants/:tenantId/members` | `parseInt(tenantId) !== tid` check | 2736 |
+| `PATCH /api/tenants/:tenantId/members/:userId/role` | `parseInt(tenantId) !== tid` check | 2756 |
+| `DELETE /api/tenants/:tenantId/members/:userId` | `parseInt(tenantId) !== tid` check | 2779 |
+| All invitation endpoints | `parseInt(tenantId) !== tid` check | 2872, 2895, 2913 |
+
+No shared tenant ID is used as a substitute for real tenancy — every credential/membership is tied to an explicit tenant from the JWT claim.
+
+### Database-Verified RBAC — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- `tenant_memberships` table with `role` column (server.js:411–425)
+- `requireRole("owner", "admin")` middleware enforces role-based access (server.js:2732, 2750, 2773)
+- Membership revocation takes effect immediately (no caching of role in token)
+- Last-owner protection: cannot remove self if sole owner (server.js:2782–2789)
+- Member role change protected to `owner` only (server.js:2750)
+
+
+### Invitation Token Security — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- **Generation:** `randomBytes(32).toString("hex")` — 256-bit entropy (server.js:2859–2860)
+- **Expiry:** 7-day TTL from creation (server.js:2876)
+- **Replay prevention:** Token checked for `revoked`, `accepted_at`, and `expires_at` before acceptance (server.js:2962–2964)
+- **Single acceptance:** `accepted_at` set on accept; subsequent accepts rejected with 410 (server.js:2963, 2985)
+- **Revocation:** `revoked = true` flag prevents acceptance (server.js:2917, 2962)
+- **Cross-tenant:** Invitations bound to specific `tenant_id` (server.js:2878)
+
+### Secret Sanitization — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- `SENSITIVE_KEYS` set includes: secret, token, password, credential, ciphertext, apikey, api_key, authorization, private_key, access_token, refresh_token (server.js:2804–2816)
+- `sanitizeMetadata` recursively redacts matching keys to `[REDACTED]` (server.js:2818–2836)
+- Case-insensitive matching via `keyLower.includes(s)` (server.js:2827)
+- Handles nested objects and arrays (verified by audit.test.js)
+- `sanitizeCredentialRow` never returns `ciphertext`, `iv`, `auth_tag`, or `key_version` (server.js:2524–2537)
+- Audit errors logged without secrets: `logger.error({ error: err.message }, ...)` only (server.js:2846)
+
+### Authentication, Authorization, Rate Limiting — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- `requireAuth` verifies JWT with `tenant_id` claim (existing on feature branch)
+- `requireRole("owner", "admin")` on sensitive endpoints (server.js:2732, 2750, 2773, 2863, 2891, 2909)
+- `credentialLimiter`: 30 requests/minute (server.js:2508–2514)
+- `membershipLimiter`: 30 requests/minute (server.js:2713–2719)
+- `invitationLimiter`: 20 requests/minute (server.js:2851–2857)
+- All endpoints wrapped in try/catch with generic error messages (no stack traces to client)
+
+### SQL Injection and Input Validation — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- All database queries use parameterized `$1, $2, ...` placeholders (no string interpolation in SQL)
+- Provider names validated against `ALLOWED_CREDENTIAL_PROVIDERS` allow-list (server.js:2516–2522, 2545–2546)
+- Role values validated against `["owner", "admin", "member", "viewer"]` (server.js:2758, 2869)
+- Password minimum length 6 chars (server.js:2952)
+- Email required for invitations (server.js:2868)
+- Username validated on registration (existing code)
+
+### Production/Test Database Separation — VERIFIED ✅
+
+- Fail-closed guard in `start()`: `NODE_ENV=test` requires DATABASE_URL containing `_test` or `test` (server.js:3047–3052)
+- CI uses `lead_pipeline_test` database name (.github/workflows/ci.yml:10)
+- Test-only JWT_SECRET and ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY in CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml:12–13)
+- Production enforcement: `ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY` must be 32-byte base64 (server.js:521–526); `JWT_SECRET` must be ≥32 chars and not weak (server.js:475–478)
+
+### Vulnerabilities by Severity
+
+| Severity | Issue | File:Line |
+|---|---|---|
+| LOW | CI `ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY` committed in plaintext (test-only key) | `.github/workflows/ci.yml:13` |
+| MEDIUM | CI `JWT_SECRET` committed in plaintext (test-only secret) | `.github/workflows/ci.yml:12` |
+| MEDIUM | CI service creates `lead_pipeline` DB but app connects to `lead_pipeline_test` — migration must create the test DB | `.github/workflows/ci.yml:10,25` |
+| LOW | Credential validation calls external provider domains via `safeFetch` — SSRF already protected | `server.js:2683–2685` |
+
+
