+## 5. Complete RBAC and database-verified membership
+
+### Existing implementation and file paths
+- **Feature branch (aa1f0e1):** `users.role` column (default `'owner'`), `requireRole(...roles)` middleware returns 403 if caller's role not in list. `users.tenant_id` FK to `tenants`.
+- **Missing:** role is set only at registration (`'owner'` default); no way to change roles, no membership table for users belonging to multiple tenants, no DB-verified membership checks beyond the token claim, no role hierarchy, no fine-grained permissions.
+
+### Missing functionality
+- No membership table (user↔tenant many-to-many with role per membership).
+- No endpoint to list/update/remove members of a tenant.
+- No endpoint to change a user's role within a tenant.
+- `requireAuth` trusts the JWT `tenant_id` claim without verifying against a membership table at request time (token could be stale after membership revocation).
+- No fine-grained RBAC (read/write/admin per resource).
+
+### Proposed changes
+- New table `tenant_memberships`: `id SERIAL PK`, `tenant_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id)`, `user_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id)`, `role TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'member'` (e.g. 'owner','admin','member','viewer'), `created_at`, `invited_by_user_id`, unique `(tenant_id, user_id)`, indexes on `(tenant_id)` and `(user_id)`.
+- Backfill: existing users with `tenant_id` get a membership row with their current role.
+- `requireAuth` enhanced: verify `req.user.tenant_id` corresponds to an active `tenant_memberships` row for `req.user.id` (DB-verified membership), reject 401/403 if membership missing or revoked.
+- `requireRole(role)` checks membership role, not just token claim.
+- API (additive, behind `requireAuth` + appropriate role):
+  - `GET /api/tenants/:tenantId/members` — list members (owner/admin only).
+  - `PATCH /api/tenants/:tenantId/members/:userId/role` — change role (owner only).
+  - `DELETE /api/tenants/:tenantId/members/:userId` — remove member (owner only; cannot remove self if last owner).
+
+### Database migrations
+- `tenant_memberships` table; backfill script in migration; indexes.
+
+### API changes
+- New `/api/tenants/:tenantId/members/*` endpoints — additive.
+- Existing endpoints unchanged (non-breaking) but `requireAuth` now also verifies membership DB row (behavior change: stale tokens after removal are rejected — document as security improvement).
+
+### Security considerations
+- Membership revocation takes effect immediately (DB check per request), not only at token expiry.
+- Owner cannot remove themselves if they are the sole owner (prevent tenant lockout).
+- Role changes reflected immediately.
+- Do not leak membership existence for tenants the caller doesn't belong to (404 vs 403 consistency).
+
+### Tests required
+- Unit tests: `requireRole` with various roles; membership verification accept/reject.
+- Integration tests: create tenant B members, user B role changes, revoked membership immediately rejected, sole-owner self-removal blocked, cross-tenant member listing rejected.
