+## 12. Migration and rollback strategy
+
+### Existing implementation and file paths
+- **Feature branch:** schema changes are inline in `server.js` `initDb()` (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + ad-hoc `ALTER TABLE` + backfill `UPDATE ... SET tenant_id = 1`). No versioned migration files, no migration runner, no rollback scripts.
+
+### Missing functionality
+- No versioned migrations, no migration tracking table, no rollback path, no way to apply migrations separately from server startup.
+
+### Proposed changes
+- Introduce a simple migration table `schema_migrations` (`version TEXT PRIMARY KEY`, `applied_at TEXT`).
+- Create versioned migration SQL files under a `migrations/` directory (e.g. `001_initial.sql`, `002_tenant_credentials.sql`, ... `00X_phase_a5.sql`).
+- Each Phase A.5 component gets its own migration:
+  - `00X_encryption_keys.sql` — `encryption_keys` table.
+  - `00X_tenant_credentials.sql` — `tenant_credentials` table + indexes.
+  - `00X_tenant_memberships.sql` — `tenant_memberships` + backfill.
+  - `00X_tenant_invitations.sql` — `tenant_invitations`.
+  - `00X_audit_log.sql` — `audit_log`.
+  - `00X_schema_migrations.sql` — tracking table.
+- `initDb()` applies pending migrations in order (idempotent `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` inside each, plus tracking inserts).
+- Rollback: provide `down` SQL per migration (DROP TABLE / ALTER TABLE reverse) documented in migration files; rollback executed manually via a CLI command or migration tool, not auto-run (to avoid accidental data loss). For small deployments, document manual rollback steps.
+- Backward compatibility: new tables/columns are additive; existing queries keep working. `tenant_credentials`, `tenant_memberships`, `tenant_invitations`, `audit_log`, `encryption_keys` are all new tables — no breaking changes to existing tables beyond what aa1f0e1 already did (composite PK on businesses).
+
+### Database migrations
+- New `migrations/` directory with numbered SQL files; `schema_migrations` tracking table.
+
+### API changes
+- None (migration is internal).
+
+### Security considerations
+- Migrations must not log secret values.
+- Rollback of `tenant_credentials` destroys credentials — document as destructive.
+- Test migrations run against `lead_pipeline_test` only.
+
+### Tests required
+- Test that migrations are idempotent (run twice, no error).
+- Test that `schema_migrations` tracks applied versions.
+- Test rollback SQL is syntactically valid (dry-run).
+
+### Dependencies
+- None new (uses `pg`); no migration library to keep dependency footprint small for free deployments.
+
+### Implementation order
+- Migrations created alongside each component; `schema_migrations` first.
+
+### Acceptance criteria
+- `initDb()` applies all migrations idempotently.
+- Fresh test DB + migrations + seed produces a working server.
+- Rollback SQL documented per migration.
